[patterns/application/micro-frontend/PTN-APP-MFE-010-event-bus-communication-pattern.md#anti-patterns]

### Anti-Patterns

**❌ Anti-Pattern 1: Synchronous Request-Response via Events**

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS - Event Bus is fire-and-forget
eventBus.publish('fetch-user', { userId: '123' });

// Wait for response event? NO!
eventBus.subscribe('user-fetched', (user) => {
  setUser(user);  // No guarantees this happens; timing issues
});
```

**✅ Correct Approach**: Use Backend API for request-response; use Event Bus for notifications.

**❌ Anti-Pattern 2: Large Event Payloads**

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS - Payloads should be small
eventBus.publish('claim.submitted', {
  claim: fullClaimObject,  // 500KB object!
  member: fullMemberObject,  // 200KB object!
  provider: fullProviderObject,  // 150KB object!
});
```

**✅ Correct Approach**: Publish IDs only; subscribers fetch full data from backend if needed.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Minimal event payload
eventBus.publish('claim.submitted', {
  claimId: 'claim-123',
  memberId: 'member-123',
  providerId: 'provider-123',
});

// Subscriber fetches full data if needed
async function handleClaimSubmitted(event) {
  const claim = await claimsApi.getClaim(event.claimId);
  // ...
}
```

**❌ Anti-Pattern 3: Throwing Errors from Subscribers**

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER DO THIS - Throwing doesn't help anyone
eventBus.subscribe('claim.submitted', async (event) => {
  const result = await processEvent(event);
  if (!result.success) {
    throw new Error('Processing failed');  // Publisher doesn't see this!
  }
});
```

**✅ Correct Approach**: Log errors, report to error tracking, but don't throw.

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Log errors, don't throw
eventBus.subscribe('claim.submitted', async (event) => {
  try {
    await processEvent(event);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Processing failed:', error);
    Sentry.captureException(error, { extra: { event } });
    // Don't throw
  }
});
```

