#### After: Event Bus Communication (Recommended Pattern)

**Claims Module (After):**

```typescript
// claims-mfe/src/services/claimService.ts (NEW - EVENT BUS)
async function submitClaim(claimData) {
  const claim = await claimsApi.submit(claimData);

  // Publish event (fire-and-forget, non-blocking)
  eventBus.publish<ClaimSubmittedEvent>({
    type: 'claim.submitted',
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    claimId: claim.id,
    memberId: claim.memberId,
    providerId: claim.providerId,
    claimAmount: claim.totalAmount,
    submittedBy: currentUser.id,
  });

  return claim;  // Returns immediately; downstream processing happens asynchronously
}

// Benefits:
// 1. No imports from other modules; zero build-time dependencies
// 2. New subscribers added without modifying Claims code
// 3. Immediate return; user sees success message in <1s
// 4. Event logged for audit trail
```

**Care Coordination Module (After):**

```typescript
// carecoord-mfe/src/hooks/useClaimEventListener.ts (NEW - SUBSCRIBER)
export function useClaimEventListener() {
  const eventBus = useEventBus();

  useEffect(() => {
    const unsubscribe = eventBus.subscribe<ClaimSubmittedEvent>(
      'claim.submitted',
      async (event) => {
        try {
          console.log('Claim submitted, triggering care gap analysis:', event.claimId);
          await careGapService.analyze(event.memberId);
        } catch (error) {
          console.error('Care gap analysis failed:', error);
          Sentry.captureException(error, { extra: { event } });
          // Error doesn't affect Claims module
        }
      }
    );

    return unsubscribe;
  }, [eventBus]);
}

// Benefits:
// 1. No exports needed; Care Coord doesn't expose API to other modules
// 2. Independent deployment; can update subscriber logic without affecting Claims
